{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1657 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "331fccc8031e1810bf9f5ab17702d24d7c3a23093efe13c7c218f4c1e35da6f1" :edb/db-before-t 1656 :edb/db-after-t 1657 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534969 50 #inst "2026-10-08T12:32:33.934Z" 13194139534969 true] [17592186133489 1100 "Given ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/eec8345a2a1eb622aafae6890c6548efcd5b595d18334b5bad9e43f8b0fd4534.png) find $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|.$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186133489 1100 "Given $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$ find $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|$." 13194139534969 false] [17592186133489 1145 "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖x‖ &= \\sqrt{x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2} + x_{3}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3^{2} + (-4)^{2} + (-5)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9 + 16 + 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{50} \\\\\n&= 5\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534969 false] [17592186133489 1145 "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186133490 1100 "Given the vectors ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/c3261bc45f978551da6b9ae98489e4eeceadfb5a4669a703736b3d623ed2c41d.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/40f7e2f6c5aaff24c18d65776fbbb62f44effeb921bc6e54a4e4f7ada905e614.png) find the distance $\\text{d}(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}).$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186133490 1100 "Given the vectors $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ find the distance $\\text{d}(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y})$." 13194139534969 false] [17592186133490 1145 "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd(x, y) &= ‖x - y‖ \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(x_{1} - y_{1})^{2} + (x_{2} - y_{2})^{2} + (x_{3} - y_{3})^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-1 - 2)^{2} + (2 - 0)^{2} + (3 - (-1))^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-3)^{2} + 2^{2} + 4^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9 + 4 + 16} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{29}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534969 false] [17592186133490 1145 "Using the formula for the distance, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1-2)^{2}+(2-0)^{2}+(3-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186133491 1100 "Normalize the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044632/assets/33fcf438acd77616d7f5c6881234f9dcc87136575b741af6af72eee9d4401dfb.png)" 13194139534969 true] [17592186133491 1100 "Normalize the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534969 false] [17592186133491 1145 "To normalize a vector $\\mathbf{x}$, we have to divide the vector by its norm:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\mathbf{x}}{\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to normalize $\\mathbf{x}$, we first calculate $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖x‖ &= \\sqrt{x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-8)^{2} + 6^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{64 + 36} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{100} \\\\\n&= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $\\mathbf{x}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x}{‖x‖} &= \\frac{x}{10} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}x \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{-8}{10} \\\\ \\frac{6}{10}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534969 false] [17592186133491 1145 "To normalize a vector $\\mathbf{x},$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\dfrac{\\mathbf{x}}{\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|}.$ Therefore, to normalize $\\mathbf{x},$ we first calculate $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $\\mathbf{x}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8}{10} \\\\ \\frac{6}{10}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186133562 1100 "If $\\left\\Vert {- \\dfrac{ \\mathbf{x} }{2} } \\right\\Vert = 5,$ find $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert.$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186133562 1100 "If $\\left\\Vert {-\\dfrac{\\mathbf{x}}{2}} \\right\\Vert = 5$, find $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert$." 13194139534969 false] [17592186133562 1145 "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\\Vert k \\mathbf{x} \\Vert= \\vert k \\vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{x} \\Vert\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $\\Vert x \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖- \\frac{x}{2}‖ &= 5 \\\\\n‖- \\frac{1}{2}x‖ &= 5 \\\\\n\\mid - \\frac{1}{2} \\mid \\cdot ‖x‖ &= 5 \\\\\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot ‖x‖ &= 5 \\\\\n‖x‖ &= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖3x‖ &= 3 \\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 10 \\\\\n&= 30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534969 false] [17592186133562 1145 "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\\Vert k \\mathbf{x} \\Vert= \\vert k \\vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{x} \\Vert\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $\\Vert x \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-\\frac{x}{2}‖ & =5 \\\\ ‖-\\frac{1}{2}x‖ & =5 \\\\ |-\\frac{1}{2}|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ‖x‖ & =5 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3x‖ & =3\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =3\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186133682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323488 13194139534969 true] [17592186133682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323544 13194139534969 true] [17592186133682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323551 13194139534969 true] [17592186133683 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323495 13194139534969 true] [17592186133683 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323502 13194139534969 true] [17592186133683 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323516 13194139534969 true] [17592186133683 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323523 13194139534969 true] [17592186133683 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323558 13194139534969 true] [17592186133684 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323537 13194139534969 true] [17592186133684 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323586 13194139534969 true] [17592186133684 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323593 13194139534969 true] [17592186133684 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323600 13194139534969 true] [17592186133747 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323509 13194139534969 true] [17592186133747 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323530 13194139534969 true] [17592186133747 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323565 13194139534969 true] [17592186133747 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323572 13194139534969 true] [17592186133747 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323579 13194139534969 true] [17592186134126 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534969 true] [17592186134126 1100 "Given $x = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, find $‖x‖$." 13194139534969 false] [17592186134126 1100 "Given $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖x‖.$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186134126 1145 "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186134129 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139