3 1113 #uuid "1d8008bb-a2a5-505a-9588-d2adba2b74d2" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323593 1145 "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+0+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323595 13194139534969 true] [17592186323594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323596 13194139534969 true] [17592186323594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323597 13194139534969 true] [17592186323594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323598 13194139534969 true] [17592186323594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323599 13194139534969 true] [17592186323594 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534969 true] [17592186323594 1041 "selection" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323594 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323596 13194139534969 true] [17592186323594 1110 #uuid "08f557b4-83d0-5a22-a870-272fa05719ea" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323595 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534969 true] [17592186323595 1111 #uuid "fda996af-f034-58cf-9e84-9168239fd44d" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323596 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323596 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534969 true] [17592186323596 1111 #uuid "d1080d30-e708-5f1a-8556-d7750c6a76e4" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323597 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534969 true] [17592186323597 1111 #uuid "b24e16e3-76af-5be1-9e35-be16c50f7460" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323598 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534969 true] [17592186323598 1111 #uuid "4d7ceb31-5bd3-5fe0-b12b-a7a5bfc9621f" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323599 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534969 true] [17592186323599 1111 #uuid "207e7f9f-285d-59d0-a8ed-6c5d19219205" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323600 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323601 13194139534969 true] [17592186323600 1089 "q-74151" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323600 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534969 true] [17592186323600 1100 "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -k \\\\ 2k \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $k$, if the distance between the vectors is $\\text{d}(x,y)=2\\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323600 1113 #uuid "de94dd8c-d1ac-5e3c-a7d7-a9749972614e" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323600 1145 "First, we calculate the distance between $x$ and $y$ in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{y}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-k)^{2}+(-k-(-1))^{2}+(2k-0)^{2}+(0-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9-6k+{k}^{2}+{k}^{2}-2k+1+4{k}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $\\text{d}(x,y)=2\\sqrt{3},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14} & =2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}-8k+14})}^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2} \\\\ 6{k}^{2}-8k+14 & =12 \\\\ 6{k}^{2}-8k+2 & =0 \\\\ 3{k}^{2}-4k+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quadratic formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(3)(1)}}{2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{4}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 2}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives $k=1$ and $k=\\frac{1}{3}.$" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323602 13194139534969 true] [17592186323601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323603 13194139534969 true] [17592186323601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323604 13194139534969 true] [17592186323601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323605 13194139534969 true] [17592186323601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323606 13194139534969 true] [17592186323601 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534969 true] [17592186323601 1041 "selection" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323601 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323604 13194139534969 true] [17592186323601 1110 #uuid "eaffc6b1-18c1-5c41-b5b7-ae198f92e213" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323602 1034 "k=\\pm 1" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534969 true] [17592186323602 1111 #uuid "73f88d75-56fc-5830-abd9-8918045eb899" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323603 1034 "k=\\pm 3" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534969 true] [17592186323603 1111 #uuid "4ec84d28-276b-55d4-b8cc-6076ca3122fa" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323604 1034 "k=1,\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534969 true] [17592186323604 1111 #uuid "9ed552b7-4a5c-5857-8596-4be1bfd1eaa5" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323605 1034 "k=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534969 true] [17592186323605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534969 true] [17592186323605 1111 #uuid "de0660c8-d521-5633-b919-aebad0d3d770" 13194139534969 tr